videos.script:
Lesson 1 built the planner for a browser. Today it becomes an Android project and an iOS project, without one line of it changing. {{projects}}

Capacitor does that. It writes two real native projects, the kind Android Studio and Xcode open, and copies your built site into each. {{copy}} On the phone, a WebView shows your site, served from the app's own files. {{bridge}} And a bridge lets your code call native code, which lesson 4 uses.

You will add two packages and one file. {{init}} You will choose the app's identity, which is the one decision here you cannot take back. {{appid}} And you will meet the habit this whole course depends on: build, then sync, every time. {{loop}} Skip either step and the phone runs an old app, and nothing tells you.
